   "subject": "adjust.methylC",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am interested in using the adjust.methylC function, but after reading the documentation on\r\n<a href=\"http://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350971000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Ey43YZBsTaYuIlczx8_9q\">\r\nhttp://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">am confused about the input data sets:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Base resolution oxBS-seq data (5mC only) and BS-seq data (5hmC+5mC) from the same sample for multiple individuals.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">So essentially I have pure 5mC data but don’t have 5hmC on its own and I want to know the difference in 5hmC between two samples at single CG sites:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">How would one use the adjust.methylC function in order to obtain 5hmC only information in order to compare 2 or more different individuals?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Michelle Johnson, PhD<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Research Associate<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology<br>\r\nUniversity of Cambridge Clinical School<br>\r\nBox 223, The Rosie Hospital<br>\r\nRobinson Way<br>\r\nCambridge CB2 0SW<br>\r\nUnited Kingdom<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><a href=\"http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350971000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fyv3FcaE7xhLyN6l2A-WE\">http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><a href=\"http://mdj...@medschl.cam.ac.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mdj...@medschl.cam.ac.uk&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350971000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0BBL5SPNIzPG8Wr50IYRbf\">md...@medschl.cam.ac.uk</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><img border=\"0\" width=\"192\" height=\"46\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion/attach/ccd1fd796eed56a1/image001.gif?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"UCamblogo\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Xpa6EIikGWUJ",
   "from": "Altuna Akalin",
   "author": "ab8277113f65c05e",
   "date": "2014-08-13T12:40:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] adjust.methylC",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I think it would make sense to change the documentation at some point, you can use that function to get 5hmC levels if you have true 5mC levels.<div><br></div><div>below I changed the arguments to more appropriate versions.</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The following will give you true_5mC if you have 5hmC+5mC  and true_5hmC</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">true_5mC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">adjust</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">methylC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mcANDhmc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">true_hmc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div>or to get true 5hmC levels from  5hmC+5mC  and true_5mC</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">true_5hmC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">adjust</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">methylC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mcANDhmc </span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> true_mc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>the function adjusts methylated C counts in the object passed by first argument based on the second argument, First argument is basically should be 5mC+5hmC</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Altuna</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Aug 13, 2014 at 2:06 PM, Michelle Johnson <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">md...@medschl.cam.ac.uk</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am interested in using the adjust.methylC function, but after reading the documentation on\r\n<a href=\"http://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350973000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Z0vguPlSuzVbJWBNOX355\">\r\nhttp://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">am confused about the input data sets:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Base resolution oxBS-seq data (5mC only) and BS-seq data (5hmC+5mC) from the same sample for multiple individuals.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">So essentially I have pure 5mC data but don’t have 5hmC on its own and I want to know the difference in 5hmC between two samples at single CG sites:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">How would one use the adjust.methylC function in order to obtain 5hmC only information in order to compare 2 or more different individuals?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Michelle Johnson, PhD<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Research Associate<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology<br>\r\nUniversity of Cambridge Clinical School<br>\r\nBox 223, The Rosie Hospital<br>\r\nRobinson Way<br>\r\nCambridge CB2 0SW<br>\r\nUnited Kingdom<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><a href=\"http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350973000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3H52VuiVB2IuxiAlwOHsNT\">http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><a href=\"http://mdj...@medschl.cam.ac.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mdj...@medschl.cam.ac.uk&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350973000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1O404RLcHeUNqpVIPe0B21\">md...@medschl.cam.ac.uk</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><img border=\"0\" width=\"192\" height=\"46\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion/attach/6519a48810ba965e/image001.gif?part=0.1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"UCamblogo\"><span><font color=\"#888888\"><u></u><u></u></font></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n</font></span></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
