     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am interested in using the adjust.methylC function, but after reading the documentation on\r\n<a href=\"http://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350974000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PpQgIXarDOyoFz-29FiDp\">\r\nhttp://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/methylKit/functions/adjust.methylC</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">am confused about the input data sets:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Base resolution oxBS-seq data (5mC only) and BS-seq data (5hmC+5mC) from the same sample for multiple individuals.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">So essentially I have pure 5mC data but don’t have 5hmC on its own and I want to know the difference in 5hmC between two samples at single CG sites:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">How would one use the adjust.methylC function in order to obtain 5hmC only information in order to compare 2 or more different individuals?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Michelle Johnson, PhD<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Research Associate<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology<br>\r\nUniversity of Cambridge Clinical School<br>\r\nBox 223, The Rosie Hospital<br>\r\nRobinson Way<br>\r\nCambridge CB2 0SW<br>\r\nUnited Kingdom<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><a href=\"http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350974000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2yeQCSr9lm5xZTP7Ga7MDG\">http://www.trophoblast.cam.ac.uk/people/JohnsonMichelle.shtml</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><a href=\"http://mdj...@medschl.cam.ac.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mdj...@medschl.cam.ac.uk&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234350974000&amp;usg=AOvVaw069uufs182ddHmeTrq23k5\">md...@medschl.cam.ac.uk</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><img border=\"0\" width=\"192\" height=\"46\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion/attach/54c8f383f96d7fa5/image001.gif?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"UCamblogo\"><span><font color=\"#888888\"><u></u><u></u></font></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoN